" height=\"244\" data-attachment-id=\"746\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/shaoyiwang.com\/?attachment_id=746\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/shaoyiwang.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/09\/2-9.png?fit=950%2C244&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"950,244\" data-comments-opened=\"0\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"2-9\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/shaoyiwang.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/09\/2-9.png?fit=950%2C244&amp;ssl=1\" data-id=\"746\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/shaoyiwang.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/09\/2-9.png?resize=950%2C244&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-746\" srcset=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/shaoyiwang.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/09\/2-9.png?w=950&amp;ssl=1 950w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/shaoyiwang.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/09\/2-9.png?resize=300%2C77&amp;ssl=1 300w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/shaoyiwang.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/09\/2-9.png?resize=768%2C197&amp;ssl=1 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 950px) 100vw, 950px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center wp-block-paragraph\">.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Bells &amp; Whistles<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">To explore the effect of color in hybrid images, I compared four different cases: using grayscale for both inputs, adding color only to the low-frequency image, adding color only to the high-frequency image, and keeping both inputs in color.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">From the results, adding color to the low-frequency image makes the hybrid look clearer and closer to a normal picture, especially when viewed from far away. Adding color only to the high-frequency image does not change much, since edges and fine details do not benefit a lot from color. When both images are in color, the result looks almost the same as when only the low-frequency one is in color. It works better to have the color in low frequencies!<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-gallery has-nested-images columns-4 is-cropped wp-block-gallery-9 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"292\" height=\"409\" data-attachment-id=\"748\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/shaoyiwang.com\/?attachment_id=748\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/shaoyiwang.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/09\/2-10-1.png?fit=292%2C409&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"292,409\" data-comments-opened=\"0\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"2-10-1\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/shaoyiwang.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/09\/2-10-1.png?fit=292%2C409&amp;ssl=1\" data-id=\"748\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/shaoyiwang.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/09\/2-10-1.png?resize=292%2C409&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-748\" srcset=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/shaoyiwang.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/09\/2-10-1.png?w=292&amp;ssl=1 292w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/shaoyiwang.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/09\/2-10-1.png?resize=214%2C300&amp;ssl=1 214w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 292px) 100vw, 292px\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<figure class