g.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/09\/2-18-1.png?resize=300%2C59&amp;ssl=1 300w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/shaoyiwang.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/09\/2-18-1.png?resize=768%2C150&amp;ssl=1 768w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/shaoyiwang.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/09\/2-18-1.png?resize=1536%2C300&amp;ssl=1 1536w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/shaoyiwang.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/09\/2-18-1.png?resize=1200%2C235&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/shaoyiwang.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/09\/2-18-1.png?w=1570&amp;ssl=1 1570w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 1000px\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">By applying this blurred mask to each level of the Laplacian stack, I got the following results, which combine the two inputs into a smooth blend (the \u201cOraple\u201d).<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-large is-resized\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"510\" height=\"1024\" data-attachment-id=\"781\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/shaoyiwang.com\/?attachment_id=781\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/shaoyiwang.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/09\/2-18.png?fit=940%2C1888&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"940,1888\" data-comments-opened=\"0\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"2-18\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/shaoyiwang.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/09\/2-18.png?fit=510%2C1024&amp;ssl=1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/shaoyiwang.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/09\/2-18.png?resize=510%2C1024&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-781\" sty